obs the harness moved that foreground pass to the background at its 600s timeout and its pipe to `tail` withheld every byte until EOF, so the run read as silent for twenty-five minutes while the pid was alive the whole time; the lock file named the pid and answered it. Next cold pass writes to session-output/ rather than through a pipe.
think reds first: the pin itself was the block. tools/fixtures/r/reds_pin_capacity_scan.sh read pin_bytes=40949 of 40960, rows_that_fit=0, pin_foldable_rows=1 -- eight ships sharing a ledger that could accept no red at all
obs that is the discipline stopped by the file that carries it, and the lawful move was already named by the tree: door B (20260829) folds a BOOKED row, and exactly one stood
obs this lap folded %623 onto a shelf of its own to make that room -- pin 40949 -> 38001, rows_that_fit 0 -> 1 -- and the rebase found the row's own seat had folded it upstream in the same hour, onto construction/archive/REDS-a-seat-named-in-four-places-rows-623.md. Two ships folding one row is what reds_ledger_monotone reads as rows_double_shelved, and its ceiling of 1 already carries %512 from `20260906`. My duplicate shelf and its recital line were dropped; upstream's fold stands, and the room it made is what this lap's own row landed in.
think with room made, booked the red this seat parked at 20260908.093729 and could not write down: standing_equipment reds on every DETACHED launch and greens on every hand-run one
obs the mechanism, in plain words: tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_control.sh plants a lock holder as `sleep 45 & live_holder=$!`, and a shell without job control starts no new process group, so the holder inherits the group of whatever launched the control. A lap that launches its roster pass detached exits while the twenty-five-minute pass runs on, the group leader is gone, the plant answers live_group_plant=unavailable, and tools/s/standing_equipment_witness.rish:415 asserts live_group_plant=ok and knows no third answer.
obs the abstention is worth keeping -- the control's own comment says a reading proven only where it fires cannot be told from one stuck on -- so the repair took the CAUSE rather than teaching the witness to accept a third word
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_control.sh `set -m` wraps the one background command and `set +m` follows it; POSIX job control puts each background job in a process group of its own, so the holder leads its own group and depends on no launcher. Job control goes off again immediately because it also changes how a background child takes SIGINT and SIGQUIT.
think proved it on metal in a throwaway shell first: with `set -m` the holder's pgid equals its own pid, without it the pgid is the launcher's, in a detached shell and a live one alike
obs proven from both sides on the real control under a launcher that dies -- `setsid sh -c 'nohup sh <control> > out 2>&1 & exit'` reads live_group_plant=unavailable at f16c05934 and ok with the repair; the whole witness, which reddened under that launch, closes GREEN under it
file construction/REDS.md row booked and CLOSED at stamp 20260908.093729; the number derived %630 after `git fetch xy`, and the rebase found peers had published %630, %631, %632 and %633 while this lap ran, so it renumbered to %634 -- the stamp is the key, and the move cost one line because every living citation already spelled the stamp. Folded the same hour so the pin can accept the next red.
file construction/archive/REDS-the-third-answer-a-witness-did-not-know-rows-634.md new shelf for the row; rows_that_fit back to 1 with the row on it
file construction/ITINERARY.md COPAL block rewritten, elder shelved, the card's own bound surfaced
file construction/archive/20260908-104016_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the elder COPAL block kept whole
obs the air walk found nothing loose in my own lane, and that is a reading rather than an empty lap: amphora's cross-roof orders carry `couples:` and `covers:` markers AND comptime asserts in the same files, amphora/src/manifest_entry.rye is a symlink rather than a copy, and bron-resins/manifest.bron's *Bron only* law names its one .md exception in its own note line
obs one fence beside them, measured rather than assumed: TAME_CORE's *prefer tally/kumara.rye over bare Ed25519* has no instrument and wants none -- all 27 tracked .rye reaching std.crypto.sign.Ed25519 are the canon itself or crypto/'s own implementation. Its sibling *prefer tally/parse_int.rye* has one, tools/t/tame_style_scan_advise.rish, and 42 application sites stand.
